        "body": "Fixes #84\n\n## Summary\n\nAdds a concise `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` so new pull requests are pre-populated with prompts that match the project's contribution guidelines.\n\n## Motivation\n\nIssue #84 notes that the repository has no PR template, while AGENTS.md already requires impact descriptions, validation commands, issue links, and UI screenshots. Contributors currently receive no guided prompts when opening a PR.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Single file: `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`\n- Prompts cover: summary (before/after), linked issue, affected surfaces, exact validation commands/results (without forcing full suites for trivial changes), screenshots for UI changes, and explicit boundary notes for RF/scope/persistence/compatibility changes.\n- Aligns with AGENTS.md and the Unreleased/VERSION changelog policy.\n- No CI, CODEOWNERS, or merge-policy changes.\n\n## Testing\n\n- File placement verified so GitHub will recognize and prepopulate the template on new PRs.\n- Markdown reviewed for clarity and completeness against the acceptance criteria in #84.\n- No code changes; no test suite execution required.\n\nPlease review and let me know if any wording should be adjusted.",
